    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d765">

                <pb facs="0931" n="849" xml:id="pg849"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 476.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 6, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of May 25, No. 325.</p>
                <p>The information which it contains seems to justify us in assuming that the French
                    government has made arrangements for withdrawing one-third of its forces now in
                    Mexico from that country in October. The knowledge of this fact will have a
                    tendency to quiet the public mind in the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
